          "code": "GENERATE_RENEWAL_BRIEF",
          "id": "1774961369213",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774961369215_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an enterprise renewal analyst.\n\nProduce a concise executive renewal brief using only the provided summary facts.\nReturn strict JSON only. No markdown.\n\nInput JSON:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_BRIEF_FACTS.$output.result}}\n\nRules:\n- Do not invent data.\n- Omit null or empty fields.\n- Do not try to enumerate every product.\n- Use only topRiskProducts when mentioning product examples.\n- If highRiskProductDisplaySummary is present, use that phrasing verbatim when describing the quantity of high-risk exposure.\n- Do not describe topRiskProducts.length as the total number of high-risk products when grouped labels include \"(N products)\".\n- Keep the brief short and executive-ready.\n\nReturn exactly this shape:\n{\n  \"Renewal Brief\": \"\",\n  \"Customer Profile\": {\n    \"Customer Name\": \"\",\n    \"Products Reviewed\": 0,\n    \"Customer Acceptance\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"Renewal Financials\": {\n    \"Current Revenue\": 0,\n    \"Total Costs\": 0,\n    \"Margin Calculated\": 0\n  },\n  \"Risk Overview\": {\n    \"Risk Profile\": \"\",\n    \"Pathway\": \"\",\n    \"Segmentation\": \"\",\n    \"Why This Pathway\": \"\",\n    \"Top Risk Products\": []\n  }\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Engagement Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779299222999"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_ENGAGEMENT_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1775121459870",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775121459872_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Customer Success renewal analyst. Generate a single narrative paragraph (100-150 words). Use natural business prose. No repetition. No bullet points.\n\nThe input facts below were derived from all unique products in the request. Use only these facts. Do not invent data.\n\nFRAMING RULES (follow the first matching case):\n\nDefine each product’s RiskProfile using the prepared input facts:\n- High if RiskCounts.High > 0\n- Medium if no High exists and RiskCounts.Medium > 0\n- Low otherwise\n\nCASE A: At least one product has RiskProfile = \"High\"\n- Introduce all products listed in HighRiskProducts together as peer drivers of renewal risk.\n- If HighRiskGroupingSummary is present, use that phrasing verbatim when describing quantity so grouped product names are not mistaken for the total number of risky product rows.\n- Do NOT mention products with RiskProfile = \"Low\".\n- For each listed high-risk product, explicitly state whether the risk is churn or financial, based only on its riskType, and include its driver.\n- If multiple listed products share the same risk type, group them naturally where possible instead of repeating identical phrasing.\n- If AdditionalHighRiskCount > 0, summarize the remainder as \"and X other high-risk products.\"\n\nCASE B: No High risks, but at least one product has RiskProfile = \"Medium\"\n- State: \"No critical risks, but [Product] requires attention due to [medium risk driver].\"\n- Use PrimaryMediumRiskProduct only.\n- Limit Medium-risk explanation to ONE short clause. Do not expand into multi-sentence analysis.\n- Do NOT mention products with RiskProfile = \"Low\".\n\nCASE C: All products have RiskProfile = \"Low\"\n- State: \"No notable risks. The renewal is on track for standard processing.\"\n- Keep to 1-2 sentences total.\n\nATTRIBUTION RULES (always follow):\n- Use the provided productName exactly.\n- financialRiskLevel = \"High\" or \"Medium\" means the product has financial risk at that level.\n- churnRiskLevel = \"High\" or \"Medium\" means the product has churn risk at that level.\n- Never assign a risk level that is not explicitly present.\n- Do not describe HighRiskProducts.length as the total number of high-risk products when grouped labels include counts such as \"(2 products)\".\n\nEXPANSION RULE:\n- Do NOT infer expansion opportunity from usage decline or churn signals.\n- Only state expansion opportunity if ExplicitExpansionSignals contains explicit growth or overage signals.\n- If no growth or overage signals exist, omit expansion entirely.\n\nCLOSING RULE:\n- End with one action sentence that prioritizes churn risk first, and includes financial risk actions if present.\n- Do not close on churn only when financial risk also exists.\n\nOUTPUT STRUCTURE:\n1. First sentence: CustomerName, RenewalDateDisplay, ContractValue.display, ContractTerm.display.\n2. Second sentence: risk framing per CASE A/B/C above.\n3. Closing: action sentence per CLOSING RULE using ActionContext.\n\nINPUT:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_ENGAGEMENT_SUMMARY_FACTS.$output.result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Normalize Request Payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const safeJsonParse = (value) => {\n  try {\n    if (value === null || value === undefined) return null;\n    if (typeof value === \"object\") return value;\n    if (typeof value !== \"string\") return null;\n    return JSON.parse(value);\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n};\n\nconst raw = $context.$triggers.REST.$input.requestPayload || {};\nconst parsed = safeJsonParse(raw) ?? raw;\nconst input =\n  parsed && parsed.requestPayload && typeof parsed.requestPayload === \"object\"\n    ? parsed.requestPayload\n    : parsed && typeof parsed === \"object\"\n      ? parsed\n      : {};\n\nconst productIdsRaw =\n  input.productId ??\n  input.ProductIds ??\n  input[\"Product Ids\"] ??\n  input[\"ProductIds\"] ??\n  [];\n\nconst productIds = Array.isArray(productIdsRaw)\n  ? productIdsRaw\n  : productIdsRaw === null || productIdsRaw === undefined || productIdsRaw === \"\"\n    ? []\n    : [productIdsRaw];\n\nconst acceptanceRaw = input.customerAcceptance ?? input[\"Customer Acceptance\"] ?? input.CustomerAcceptance;\nconst customerAcceptance = [\"y\", \"yes\", \"true\"].includes(String(acceptanceRaw ?? \"\").trim().toLowerCase())\n  ? \"Yes\"\n  : \"No\";\n\nreturn {\n  SubscriptionId: input.subscriptionId ?? input[\"Target Subscription Id\"] ?? input.SubscriptionId ?? null,\n  SubscriptionNumber: input.subscriptionNumber ?? input[\"Target Subscription Number\"] ?? input[\"Source Subscription Number\"] ?? input.SubscriptionNumber ?? null,\n  TransactionId: input.transactionId ?? input[\"Transaction Id\"] ?? input.TransactionId ?? null,\n  AdditionalInfo: input.additionalInfo ?? input[\"Additional Info\"] ?? input.AdditionalInfo ?? null,\n  CustomerAcceptance: customerAcceptance,\n  ProductIds: productIds,\n  ProductCount: productIds.length\n};"
